"Ultragenyx Announces Phase 3 Aspire results in Angelman Syndrome—Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc. (https://ir.ultragenyx.com/news-releases/news-release-details/ultragenyx-announces-phase-3-aspire-results-angelman-syndrome)\nciteturn86search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: today; 02, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc. (NASDAQ: RARE) today announced results from the Phase 3 Aspire study for apazunersen (GTX-102) in Angelman syndrome. ... Except for the historical information contained herein, the matters set forth in this press release, including statements related to Ultragenyx’s plans to evaluate its operations and implement significant expense reductions, the Company’s expectations for profitability in 2027, the expected scope, timing, benefits and impact of those actions, its future operating results and financial performance, its business plans and objectives for GTX-102 following the Aspire results, the future development and regulatory path for GTX-102, the growth and importance of its commercial business, and the potential approval and commercialization of UX111 are forward-looking statements within the meaning of the “safe harbor” provisions of the Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995.\n\nUltragenyx Announces Phase 3 Aspire results in Angelman Syndrome\n\nSeptember 2, 2026\n\nPhase 3 Aspire did not achieve the primary endpoint of change from Baseline in Bayley-4 cognitive raw score nor the key secondary endpoint of net response in Multidomain Responder Index (MDRI)\n\nNOVATO, Calif., Sept. 02, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc. (NASDAQ: RARE) today announced results from the Phase 3 Aspire study for apazunersen (GTX-102) in Angelman syndrome. The study did not achieve the primary endpoint of change from Baseline in Bayley-4 cognitive raw score nor the key secondary endpoint of net response in Multidomain Responder Index (MDRI). The safety profile observed in Aspire was consistent with Phase 1/2.\n\n“Based on everything we observed in the robust Phase 1/2 clinical development program and long-term extension study, we are disappointed by the Aspire result,” said Emil Kakkis, M.D., Ph.D., chief executive officer and president of Ultragenyx. “Even more, we are disappointed for the global patient community who has invested so much in early-stage research, working to bring a first-ever treatment to their children.”\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSEC Filing—Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc. (https://ultragenyx.gcs-web.com/node/19226/html)\nciteturn86search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: today; On September 2, 2026, Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc. (“Ultragenyx” or the “Company”) announced results from the Phase 3 Aspire study for apazunersen (GTX-102) in Angelman syndrome.\n☐\n\n## Item 8.01 Other Events.\n\nOn September 2, 2026, Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc. (“Ultragenyx” or the “Company”) announced results from the Phase 3 Aspire study for apazunersen (GTX-102) in Angelman syndrome. The study did not achieve the primary endpoint of change from Baseline in Bayley-4 cognitive raw score nor the key secondary endpoint of net response in Multidomain Responder Index (“MDRI”). The safety profile observed in Aspire was consistent with Phase 1/2.\n\nIn Aspire, the randomized groups were comparable at baseline and consistent with the patients studied in Phase 2. There were no differences between the treated and control groups that could support efficacy in the Bayley Cognition raw scores nor in the MDRI when looking at net response or mean changes of the individual five endpoints included in the MDRI.\n\nThe Company will evaluate the apazunersen program in light of this outcome and make a decision on its disposition. The Company will also assess its planned operations to define and implement significant expense reductions, while supporting its growing commercial business.\n\nSIGNATURES\n\nPursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned hereunto duly authorized.\n\n |  |  | \n   |    |    | Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc.\n   |    |    |  \nDate:  | September 2, 2026  | By:  | /s/ Howard Horn\n   |    |    | Howard Horn\nExecutive Vice President, Chief Financial Officer, Corporate Strategy--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nForm 10-Q for Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical INC filed 11/04/2026 (https://ir.ultragenyx.com/static-files/83f1b349-cb50-417a-8195-c53c514af23d)\nciteturn86search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week; **GTX-102 for the treatment of Angelman syndrome**\n\nIn September 2026, we announced results from the Phase 3 *Aspire* study for apazunersen in Angelman syndrome.\n\n**GTX-102 for the treatment of Angelman syndrome**\n\nIn September 2026, we announced results from the Phase 3 *Aspire* study for apazunersen in Angelman syndrome. The study did not achieve the primary endpoint of change from Baseline in Bayley-4 cognitive raw score nor the key secondary endpoint of net response in Multidomain Responder Index (MDRI). The safety profile observed in the *Aspire* study was consistent with Phase 1/2.\n\nIn *Aspire*, the randomized groups were comparable at baseline and consistent with the patients studied in Phase 2. There were no differences between the treated and control groups that could support efficacy in the Bayley Cognition raw scores nor in the MDRI when looking at net response or mean changes of the individual five endpoints included in the MDRI.\n\nWe are winding down this program and are working with clinical sites and patient advocacy groups to support the patient community through this transition.\n\n**Financial Operations Overview**\n\nWe are a biopharmaceutical company with a limited operating history. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1623526/000119312526437775/stok-ex99_1.htm)\nciteturn86search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: today; Stoke Therapeutics Announces Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Provides Business Updates ... The Company today reported financial results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026, and provided business updates including progress of the global Phase 3 EMPEROR study, ongoing preparations to support regulatory submissions for zorevunersen in the U.S., and the advancement of STK-002 as a potential treatment for people with Autosomal Dominant Optic Atrophy (ADOA).\n\nStoke Therapeutics Announces Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Provides Business Updates\n\n \n\n–Phase 3 EMPEROR study of zorevunersen, an investigational medicine for Dravet syndrome: ~110 patients through Week 28 primary endpoint, ~20 patients through Week 52 and all continuing into open-label treatment period; data readout anticipated in Q3 2027 followed by the planned U.S. NDA submission in H2 2027–\n\n \n\n–Successful FDA meeting to align on U.S. NDA submission: Changes in cognition and behavior, a key secondary endpoint in EMPEROR, will be analyzed using a multicomponent assessment of four Vineland-3 subdomains–\n\n \n\n–STK-002, an investigational medicine for ADOA: Dose escalation in the Phase 1 OSPREY study continues with dosing of third cohort underway; initial safety and efficacy data anticipated in H1 2027–\n\n \n\n–$358.8M in cash, cash equivalents and marketable securities as of September 30, 2026 expected to fund operations into early 2028–\n\nBEDFORD, Mass., October 29, 2026 – Stoke Therapeutics, Inc. (Nasdaq: STOK) is a biotechnology company dedicated to restoring protein expression by harnessing the body’s potential with RNA medicine and has a lead investigational medicine, zorevunersen, in development as a first-in-class potential disease-modifying treatment for Dravet syndrome. The Company today reported financial results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026, and provided business updates including progress of the global Phase 3 EMPEROR study, ongoing preparations to support regulatory submissions for zorevunersen in the U.S., and the advancement of STK-002 as a potential treatment for people with Autosomal Dominant Optic Atrophy (ADOA).\n\n \n\n“The Phase 3 EMPEROR study of zorevunersen continues to progress well. Approximately 110 of 162 enrolled patients have completed their Week 28 visit when the primary endpoint of change in major motor seizure frequency is measured and approximately 20 are through Week 52, the end of the treatment period. All 20 of these patients are continuing into the open-label extension period of the study and to date, no patients have discontinued treatment,” said Ian F. Smith, Chief Executive Officer and Director of Stoke Therapeutics. “Our NDA planning is on track following our recent discussion with the FDA. Importantly, the key secondary endpoint of changes in patients' cognition and behavior will be measured using a multicomponent assessment of four Vineland-3 subdomains. This multicomponent measure reflects the diversity of effects that people with Dravet syndrome experience and how to best evaluate them in a clinical trial. We look forward to the Phase 3 data readout in the third quarter of 2027 and completing our NDA submission in the second half of 2027.”\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStoke Therapeutics Announces Completion of Successful Meeting with the FDA to Align on Planned U.S. NDA for Zorevunersen, an Investigational Medicine for the Treatment of Dravet Syndrome - Stoke Therapeutics (https://investor.stoketherapeutics.com/news-releases/news-release-details/stoke-therapeutics-announces-completion-successful-meeting-fda)\nciteturn86search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: today; 5, 2026-- Stoke Therapeutics, Inc. ... The meeting provided an opportunity to discuss the 5 years of clinical safety and efficacy data from the Phase 1/2a and ongoing open-label extension (OLE) studies of zorevunersen and to obtain feedback on the planned NDA submission, including timing, data to be included and the analysis of Vineland-3 data, a key secondary endpoint in the Phase 3 EMPEROR study.\n\nStoke Therapeutics Announces Completion of Successful Meeting with the FDA to Align on Planned U.S. NDA for Zorevunersen, an Investigational Medicine for the Treatment of Dravet Syndrome\n\nOctober 5, 2026\n\n– Analysis of the Phase 3 EMPEROR key secondary endpoint of changes in cognition and behavior will be performed using a multicomponent assessment of four Vineland-3 subdomains –\n\n– Phase 3 readout anticipated in the third quarter of 2027 to complete the planned U.S. NDA submission in the second half of 2027 –\n\nBEDFORD, Mass.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Oct. 5, 2026-- Stoke Therapeutics, Inc. (Nasdaq: STOK) is a biotechnology company dedicated to restoring protein expression by harnessing the body’s potential with RNA medicine and has a lead investigational medicine, zorevunersen, in development as a first-in-class potential disease-modifying treatment for Dravet syndrome. The Company today announced the completion of a successful meeting with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) intended to align on key aspects of the Company’s planned submission of a New Drug Application (NDA) for zorevunersen. The meeting provided an opportunity to discuss the 5 years of clinical safety and efficacy data from the Phase 1/2a and ongoing open-label extension (OLE) studies of zorevunersen and to obtain feedback on the planned NDA submission, including timing, data to be included and the analysis of Vineland-3 data, a key secondary endpoint in the Phase 3 EMPEROR study.\n\nFollowing the discussion with the FDA, Stoke now plans to use a multicomponent assessment of four prespecified Vineland-3 subdomains to evaluate changes in cognition and behavior in the Phase 3 EMPEROR study. These four subdomains, expressive communication, receptive communication, interpersonal relationships and personal skills, were selected based on feedback from clinicians and caregivers and their potential to demonstrate meaningful effects for patients within the one-year EMPEROR treatment period. For purposes of the U.S. NDA submission, Vineland-3 subdomain data will be analyzed using a multivariate mixed model for repeated measures (MMRM).\n\nThe Company plans to continue actively engaging with the FDA and to submit data throughout the first half of 2027 to support rapid completion of the NDA submission following the Phase 3 readout anticipated in the third quarter of 2027. With these data, the Company plans to complete the U.S. NDA submission in the second half of 2027 to support a potential U.S. approval and launch of zorevunersen in early 2028.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStoke Therapeutics Announces Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Provides Business Updates - Stoke Therapeutics (https://investor.stoketherapeutics.com/news-releases/news-release-details/stoke-therapeutics-announces-third-quarter-2026-financial)\nciteturn86search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: today; The Phase 3 EMPEROR Study (NCT06872125) is a global, double-blind, sham-controlled study evaluating the efficacy, safety and tolerability of zorevunersen in children ages 2 to <18 with Dravet syndrome with a confirmed variant in the SCN1A gene not associated with gain-of-function. ... Stoke plans to submit an NDA to the FDA in the second half of 2027. Additional cohorts in Europe (Germany, France, Spain and Italy; 34 patients) and China (5 patients) completed enrollment in August and October 2026, respectively.\nAbout the Phase 3 EMPEROR Study\n\nThe Phase 3 EMPEROR Study (NCT06872125) is a global, double-blind, sham-controlled study evaluating the efficacy, safety and tolerability of zorevunersen in children ages 2 to <18 with Dravet syndrome with a confirmed variant in the SCN1A gene not associated with gain-of-function. Enrollment in the United States, United Kingdom and Japan was completed in June 2026, and a data readout is anticipated in the third quarter of 2027. Stoke plans to submit an NDA to the FDA in the second half of 2027. Additional cohorts in Europe (Germany, France, Spain and Italy; 34 patients) and China (5 patients) completed enrollment in August and October 2026, respectively.\n\nParticipants are randomized 1:1 to receive either zorevunersen via intrathecal administration or a sham comparator for a 52-week treatment period following a baseline period. The primary endpoint in the U.S. is change from baseline in log-transformed major motor seizure frequency at Week 28, although all study data will be analyzed at Week 52. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStoke Therapeutics Announces Second Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Provides Business Updates - Stoke Therapeutics (https://investor.stoketherapeutics.com/news-releases/news-release-details/stoke-therapeutics-announces-second-quarter-2026-financial/)\nciteturn86search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: today; – Phase 3 EMPEROR study of zorevunersen in Dravet syndrome: Enrollment of 162 patients complete with data readout anticipated in Q3 2027 – ... Stoke will participate in a pre-NDA meeting with the FDA during the second half of 2026 as the Company prepares to initiate the planned rolling NDA submission for zorevunersen in the first quarter of 2027.\n\nStoke Therapeutics Announces Second Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Provides Business Updates\n\nAugust 3, 2026\n\nPDF Version\n\n– Phase 3 EMPEROR study of zorevunersen in Dravet syndrome: Enrollment of 162 patients complete with data readout anticipated in Q3 2027 –\n\n– Pre-NDA meeting with FDA scheduled for H2 2026; rolling U.S. NDA submission planned to initiate in Q1 2027 –\n\n– Phase 1 OSPREY study of STK-002 in patients with ADOA: Dosing complete in sentinel cohort; dose escalation continuing and initial data anticipated in H1 2027 –\n\n– $420M in cash, cash equivalents and marketable securities based on $354.3M as of June 30, 2026 and $65.7M from a subsequent ATM sale; expected to fund operations through to potential U.S. commercialization of zorevunersen in early 2028 –\n\n– Webcast and conference call for analysts and investors at 4:30PM Eastern Time today –\n\nBEDFORD, Mass.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Aug. 3, 2026-- Stoke Therapeutics, Inc. (Nasdaq: STOK) is a biotechnology company dedicated to restoring protein expression by harnessing the body’s potential with RNA medicine and has a lead investigational medicine, zorevunersen, in development as a first-in-class potential disease-modifying treatment for Dravet syndrome. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nClinical Trials in the European Union - EMA (https://euclinicaltrials.eu/ctis-public/view/2025-523729-16-00)\nciteturn86search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Phase III clinical study of rugonersen in Angelman syndrome ... Germany  | Authorised, recruitment pending  | 26/10/2026  | 26/10/2026  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPhase III clinical study of rugonersen in Angelman syndrome\n\nEUCT number:2025-523729-16-00\n\nProtocol code:OHB-724-301\n\nTrial information\n\nMedical condition(s)Angelman syndrome\n\nTrial Phase Therapeutic confirmatory (Phase III)\n\nTransition trial No\n\nSponsor Ohb Pediatrics Limited\n\nParticipants type Pediatric, Patients\n\nAge range 0-17 years, 18-64 years\n\nLocations Germany, Italy, Spain, Netherlands, Poland\n\nMain objective To evaluate the efficacy of rugonersen compared with sham\n\nOverall Trial status\n\n[Button: Applications]\n\n | Trial  | Recruitment\n--- | --- | ---\nMember state  | Current status  | Decision date  | Last update  | Start date  | Tempo